{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% block title %}ROML model-build benchmark — summary{% endblock %}
{% block body %}
<h1>Model-construction benchmark v1</h1>
<div class="findings" style="background:#fdecea;border-color:#e3a878;">
<h2>Correction to the v1 report</h2>
<p>{{ retraction }}</p>
</div>
<p>How long does it take to <em>build</em> an equivalent linear model as the
problem grows? Two separate questions are answered on separate panels:
<strong>A. formulation</strong> (from B/T/prices or N: algebra, lowering,
and ingestion) and <strong>B. matrix ingestion</strong> (from shared
CSR/bounds/objective input). Primary metric: <code>populate_ms</code>, the
elapsed construction-API time from the first variable insertion into an
already-created empty model through objective installation. Imports, data
generation, solves, serialization, and report generation are excluded.</p>
<div class="findings">
<h2>Measured findings (paired points only)</h2>
<ul>
{% for finding in findings %}<li>{{ finding }}</li>{% endfor %}
</ul>
</div>
{% for title, div in charts %}
<div class="chart"><h2>{{ title }}</h2>{{ div | safe }}</div>
{% endfor %}
<div class="notice">
PyOptInterface is a thin direct wrapper around a HiGHS solver model, while
ROML, PuLP, and Pyomo maintain separate modeling representations. The
Populate time therefore measures elapsed user-facing construction-API work
under each library's architecture — not identical internal work. See
<a href="methodology.html">Methodology</a>.
</div>
{% endblock %}
